---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Calculator from '../../components/tools/FlightCostEstimator.jsx';
---
<BaseLayout title="Flight Cost Estimator — Quote-Based Budget Planner" description="Compare an actual airfare quote with baggage, seats, booking charges and shared airport transfers."><article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Flight Cost Estimator</h1><p class="mb-8">Compare an actual airfare quote with baggage, seats, booking charges and shared airport transfers.</p><Calculator client:load /><section class="prose max-w-none mt-10"><h2>Use your actual quotes</h2><p>Obtain a written fare quote for the exact dates, route, cabin and traveller ages. Confirm whether the price is one-way or return, what baggage is included and whether taxes are included. Enter all quoted components in the same currency.</p><h2>Compare like for like</h2><p>A low headline fare can exclude checked baggage or have different cancellation and change conditions. Record the fare rules, connection arrangements and expiry of the quote separately. This calculator adds your inputs; it does not search seats or predict airline pricing.</p><h2>Understand the result</h2><p>Per-person rows are multiplied by the traveller count; shared rows are added once. The total is divided by the number of travellers for the average per-person budget. Changing currency clears amounts because this planner does not convert prices.</p><p>For example, a shared transfer of 10,000 in the selected currency is 10,000 for the group, not 10,000 for every person. Check whether your supplier quotes per room, per traveller or for the whole group before entering a number.</p><h2>Keep a planning record</h2><p>Save the supplier name, quote date, validity, inclusions and cancellation terms with your budget. Enter zero where a cost does not apply. No unverified default fares, visa prices or insurance premiums are supplied here.</p><p>Use our <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">visa fee service</a> and <a href="/guides/">travel guides</a> for the next checks. Calculations remain in your browser.</p></section></article></BaseLayout>
